{"Title":"An Act relative to local law enforcement continuity between the city of Boston and the town of Dedham","BillNumber":"H2299","DocketNumber":"HD1264","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"R_C1","Name":"Rob Consalvo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/R_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T16:05:08.07"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"R_C1","Name":"Rob Consalvo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/R_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T16:05:08.07"},{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T12:19:41.06"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"P_M1","Name":"Paul McMurtry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/P_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T16:05:08.07"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2299/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representatives Consalvo of Boston and McMurtry of Dedham, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2299) of Rob Consalvo and Paul McMurtry relative to the authority of police officers of the city of Boston and the town of Dedham.  Public Safety and Homeland Security.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. A duly sworn officer of the Town of Dedham, who is authorized to exercise police powers within said town, may exercise all such police powers within 500 yards into the corporate limits of the City of Boston, as if such officer were a duly sworn officer of said city. \r\n\tSECTION 2. A duly sworn officer of the City of Boston, who is authorized to exercise police powers within said city, may exercise all such police powers within 500 yards into the corporate limits of the Town of Dedham, as if such officer were a duly sworn officer of said town. \r\n\tSECTION 3. This act shall take effect upon its acceptance by the City of Boston, in the manner provided by law and upon its acceptance in the Town of Dedham by a majority vote of the board of selectmen. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J22","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J22"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H36","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H36"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"S29","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S29"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}